The independent per-session PTY keeper design and strict portable protocol approach
were informed by AXXIS (https://github.com/axxis-world/axxis), copyright 2026 AXXIS
Contributors, MIT licensed. Its license is preserved in licenses/AXXIS-MIT.txt.
This repository does not incorporate AXXIS private configuration, data, or history.

portable-pty is part of WezTerm. All third-party Rust dependencies retain their
own licenses. Cargo.lock identifies the exact dependency versions of this checkout.
No endorsement by upstream projects is implied.

The VT state adapter uses alacritty_terminal from Alacritty (Apache-2.0).
Alacritty parses the screen; DOT owns sessions, protocol, transport and views.
The Android Gradle wrapper is generated by Gradle (Apache-2.0).

The authenticated IP gateway uses Rustls (Apache-2.0/ISC/MIT), ring
(ISC and other licenses in its distribution), and rcgen (MIT/Apache-2.0).
No WireGuard, Tailscale, Headscale, LocalSend or KDE Connect source is copied into
this implementation. Their designs inform the documented interoperability plan.

The desktop uses xterm.js, its fit and WebGL addons (MIT); their licenses are
preserved in licenses/xterm-MIT.txt, licenses/xterm-fit-MIT.txt and
licenses/xterm-webgl-MIT.txt. xterm.js is an independent
upstream renderer, not represented as original DOT work.
The optional iTerm2 Python library is GPL-2.0-or-later and remains a separate,
replaceable dependency. See apps/desktop/requirements-iterm.txt and its upstream
source: https://github.com/gnachman/iTerm2/tree/master/api/library/python.
Android QR scanning uses ZXing Android Embedded (Apache-2.0) and AndroidX Activity
(Apache-2.0). Rust QR generation uses qrcode (MIT/Apache-2.0).

crates/resources imports AXXIS Resource Manager collector source under MIT.
Its complete upstream license and pre-edit content hashes are stored there.
The original checkout's Git metadata was unavailable; no commit provenance is claimed.

apps/desktop/iterm_bridge.py is separately licensed GPL-2.0-or-later to match
its optional iTerm2 Python dependency. The Rust application communicates with
that bridge over JSONL pipes. No prebuilt Python dependency is checked into Git.
